' Component notes
note right of TokenBucketRateLimiterTest
  <b>Token Bucket Algorithm Tests</b>

  Comprehensive test coverage for token bucket
  rate limiting implementation.

  <b>Test Categories:</b>
  • Basic functionality (allow/deny)
  • Token refill mechanism (time-based)
  • Concurrent access (thread safety)
  • Configuration variations (parameterized)
  • Reset functionality (cleanup)
  • Edge cases (null, empty keys)

  <b>Testing Techniques:</b>
  • Nested tests for organization
  • Time-based assertions (Thread.sleep)
  • Concurrency testing (ExecutorService)
  • Parameterized tests (@ValueSource)

  <b>Total Tests:</b> 15+ test methods
end note

note bottom of SlidingWindowRateLimiterTest
  <b>Sliding Window Algorithm Tests</b>

  Focuses on sliding window specific behaviors,
  especially accuracy and boundary prevention.

  <b>Test Categories:</b>
  • Sliding window behavior
  • Accuracy tests (boundary prevention)
  • Concurrent access (thread safety)
  • Reset functionality
  • Time until next permit

  <b>Key Tests:</b>
  • shouldPreventBoundaryExploitation():
    Verifies advantage over fixed window
  • shouldGraduallyAllowRequestsAsWindowSlides():
    Tests sliding behavior over time

  <b>Testing Techniques:</b>
  • Time-based testing with delays
  • Boundary condition testing
  • Concurrency verification

  <b>Total Tests:</b> 10+ test methods
end note

note left of RateLimitFilterTest
  <b>Servlet Filter Tests</b>

  Tests HTTP integration and filter behavior.

  <b>Test Categories:</b>
  • IP-based rate limiting
  • User-based rate limiting
  • API key-based rate limiting
  • Error response format
  • Header tracking
  • Non-HTTP request handling

  <b>Mocking Strategy:</b>
  • HttpServletRequest (mock)
  • HttpServletResponse (mock)
  • FilterChain (mock)
  • PrintWriter (real, for JSON verification)

  <b>Verification:</b>
  • HTTP status codes (200, 429)
  • Response headers (X-RateLimit-*)
  • JSON error format
  • Filter chain invocation

  <b>Total Tests:</b> 12+ test methods
end note

note bottom of BasicRateLimiting
  <b>Nested Test Classes</b>

  JUnit 5 @Nested annotation provides:
  • Logical test organization
  • Separate setUp per category
  • Clear test structure in IDE
  • Better test reports

  <b>Benefits:</b>
  • Each nested class can have own @BeforeEach
  • Related tests grouped together
  • Hierarchical display in test runners
  • Easier to understand test purpose
end note

note right of Mockito
  <b>Test Doubles Framework</b>

  Mockito provides mocking capabilities:
  • Create mock objects
  • Stub method return values
  • Verify method invocations
  • Capture arguments

  <b>Usage in Tests:</b>
  • Mock HttpServletRequest/Response
  • Verify filter chain calls
  • Capture header values
  • Verify status codes

  <b>Pattern:</b>
  AAA - Arrange (mock), Act (call), Assert (verify)
end note

note left of JUnit5
  <b>Testing Framework</b>

  JUnit 5 features used:
  • @Nested: Organize related tests
  • @DisplayName: Readable test names
  • @BeforeEach: Test setup
  • @ParameterizedTest: Data-driven tests
  • Assertions: assertEquals, assertTrue, etc.

  <b>Test Lifecycle:</b>
  1. @BeforeEach runs before each test
  2. Test method executes
  3. Assertions verify behavior
  4. Cleanup (if @AfterEach)
end note

note bottom of ExecutorService
  <b>Concurrency Testing</b>

  Tests verify thread safety:
  • Multiple threads accessing same key
  • Multiple threads with different keys
  • Race condition detection
  • Atomic operation verification

  <b>Pattern:</b>
  1. Create thread pool
  2. Submit concurrent tasks
  3. Use CountDownLatch for coordination
  4. Assert expected total behavior

  <b>Verification:</b>
  Exactly N requests succeed across all threads
end note

